/-!
# Preparations for the natural-section branch of MS93 (4.4.1)

The quotient lift proves both commutator clauses from a genuine pairing seed.
The marked frame, fixed-core extension, natural Z-image and elementary seed
bounds are constructed without any trapped-radius assumption.

Final assembly still requires the favorable-orientation seed construction and
the critical-continuation argument excluding the opposite orientation. This
module does not yet assert the natural-section branch from CommonFacts alone.

Source: Meierfrankenfeld--Stellmacher (1993), printed pp.890--891.
-/
